//
// Issue #264: a SUBPIECE whose output varnode is pointer-typed (size_t *,
// unsigned int *) while the source is integer.  create_subpiece used to cast
// the integer source up to the pointer output type and then apply `>>`, which
// Sema rejects ("invalid operands to binary expression ('size_t *' and
// 'int')") — aborting CIR codegen and producing an empty translation unit.
// The fix runs the shift/mask in an unsigned-integer surrogate domain and
// converts the result back to the pointer output type (CK_IntegralToPointer).
// Here the byte offset (4) reaches the operand width (32-bit), so the extracted
// window is empty and the result is the zero pointer — emitted as a clamped
// `const 0` -> int_to_ptr rather than a poison `x >> 32`.
//
// CIR: cir.func dso_local @ecc_mul2add
// CIR: cir.cast int_to_ptr {{.*}} : !u32i -> !cir.ptr<
//
// LL:     define dso_local i32 @ecc_mul2add
// LL-DAG: store ptr null
// LL-DAG: inttoptr i32 {{.*}} to ptr
//
